---
import SiteLayout from "../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
---

<SiteLayout
  title="Milton: your instructions, in every assistant"
  description="Keep how you like things done in one place. Share your instructions with the chats and coding agents you connect."
>
  <section class="hero" aria-labelledby="headline">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">// A little less repeating yourself.</p>
      <h1 id="headline">
        Your instructions,
        <br />
        in every assistant.
      </h1>
      <p class="intro">
        Tell your assistants how you like things done. Milton keeps those
        instructions in one place, ready for the chats and coding agents you
        connect.
      </p>
      <div class="actions">
        <a class="button" href="https://app.meetmilton.com/">
          Get started <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
        </a>
        <a class="button secondary" href="#how-it-works">
          See how it works <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span>
        </a>
      </div>
      <p class="access-note">Sign in with Google or GitHub.</p>
    </div>
    <figure class="memo-example">
      <div class="sheet">
        <div class="sheet-bar">
          <span>Memo cover sheet</span>
          <span>Example instructions</span>
        </div>
        <div class="example-name">
          TPS Report <span>TPS.md</span>
        </div>
        <div class="memo-body">
          <h2>Here’s how I like to work.</h2>
          <p>Lead with the answer. Keep it short.</p>
          <p>Be direct when you disagree.</p>
          <p>Ask before taking an action I can’t undo.</p>
          <p>No em dashes. Yes to the Oxford comma.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <figcaption>
        One set of instructions for your connected assistants to read. These are
        examples, not instructions added to your account.
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
  </section>
  <div class="assistant-strip">
    <span>For the assistants you use.</span>
    <strong>Claude · ChatGPT</strong>
    <strong>Claude Code · Codex · Cursor</strong>
  </div>
  <section class="section" id="your-way">
    <p class="eyebrow">// Your way of working</p>
    <h2>From your inbox to your editor.</h2>
    <p class="section-lead">
      Keep your everyday preferences in TPS Report, your permanent core memo.
      Add a memo for the things you do a particular way.
    </p>
    <div class="use-cases">
      <article class="use-case">
        <h3>When you write and think.</h3>
        <p>
          Your tone, the detail you want, and how you like to weigh a decision.
          Bring those instructions to the next chat.
        </p>
        <p class="sample-rule">
          “Keep my emails warm, direct, and under 150 words.”
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="use-case">
        <h3>When you build.</h3>
        <p>
          How to explain a change, what to check, and when to ask before acting.
          Give each coding agent the same starting point.
        </p>
        <p class="sample-rule">
          “Explain the tradeoff before changing the approach.”
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="section" id="how-it-works">
    <p class="eyebrow">// How it works</p>
    <h2>
      Put it in writing.
      <br />
      <span>Bring it with you.</span>
    </h2>
    <ol class="steps">
      <li>
        <h3>Connect your assistants.</h3>
        <p>
          Connect Milton through your assistant’s MCP settings using{" "}
          <code>https://mcp.meetmilton.com/mcp</code>. Setup depends on the
          assistant and your plan.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>Make your preferences clear.</h3>
        <p>
          Your account starts with an empty TPS Report. Ask your connected
          assistant to help draft it from preferences you share, ask useful
          follow-ups, and show you the full draft before saving.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>Keep refining.</h3>
        <p>
          Ask your assistant to read TPS Report before it starts. Tell it what
          to change or ask it to create a memo for a task. Every saved change
          keeps a version for you to review.
        </p>
      </li>
    </ol>
    <p class="reading-note">
      Assistants still decide when to read and use your memos. Milton makes the
      instructions available; it doesn’t make the decisions for them.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="section control-section">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">// You stay in control</p>
      <h2>
        Your instructions.
        <br />
        <span>Your last word.</span>
      </h2>
    </div>
    <div class="controls">
      <article>
        <h3>See what changed.</h3>
        <p>
          Every saved change keeps a version and records who made it. Compare
          versions and restore an earlier one as a new version. The history
          stays.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <h3>Take your memos with you.</h3>
        <p>
          Download your current active memos as Markdown, including TPS.md.
          Milton’s code is open source under MIT, with instructions for running
          your own server.{" "}
          <a href="https://github.com/zoneofdanger/milton">Read the source ↗</a>
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="section faq">
    <p class="eyebrow">// A few things to know</p>
    <h2>Before you connect.</h2>
    <details>
      <summary>What is a memo?</summary>
      <p>
        A short set of written instructions for an assistant. TPS Report
        describes how you like to work in general. Other memos cover a task,
        such as your email style. TPS Report is permanent and can stay empty.
      </p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>How does this fit with an assistant’s memory?</summary>
      <p>
        Milton holds instructions about how you want things done. An assistant’s
        memory or knowledge tools can hold facts and context. You can use them
        together. Milton does not automatically import another service’s memory.
      </p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>Will an assistant always follow my memos?</summary>
      <p>
        No. They’re assistants, not employees. Milton makes your saved
        instructions available to the assistants you connect. The assistant
        still decides when to read them and how to use them. Ask it to read TPS
        Report at the start of a conversation.
      </p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>Who can read or change my memos?</summary>
      <p>
        You and the assistants you connect can read them. Assistants create and
        update content when you ask. On the website, you can archive or restore
        ordinary memos and restore earlier versions of any memo, including TPS
        Report. Archived memos are not served to assistants.{" "}
        <a href="/privacy">Read the privacy policy.</a>
      </p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>Can I try Milton?</summary>
      <p>
        Yes. <a href="https://app.meetmilton.com/">Open Milton</a> and sign in
        with Google or GitHub. New accounts start with only an empty TPS Report
        and no ordinary memos. Your connected assistant can help you write the
        first draft; approve it before saving.
      </p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>Why does this exist?</summary>
      <p>
        Peter built Milton because he was tired of asking Claude to stop using
        em dashes. Some instructions deserve a place to live outside the next
        chat.
      </p>
    </details>
  </section>
  <section class="closing">
    <p class="eyebrow">// Did you get the memo?</p>
    <h2>A better starting point.</h2>
    <p>Give your next assistant your instructions in writing.</p>
    <a class="button" href="https://app.meetmilton.com/">
      Get started <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
    </a>
  </section>
</SiteLayout>

<style>
  h1,
  h2,
  h3,
  p,
  figure {
    margin: 0;
  }
  .hero {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1.15fr 1fr;
    gap: 68px;
    align-items: center;
    padding-block: 76px 80px;
  }
  .eyebrow {
    font: 12px/1.5 var(--font-mono);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    color: var(--muted);
  }
  h1 {
    font-size: clamp(40px, 5vw, 64px);
    line-height: 1.05;
    letter-spacing: -0.035em;
    margin-top: 22px;
  }
  .intro {
    font-size: 19px;
    line-height: 1.6;
    margin-top: 24px;
    max-width: 36em;
  }
  .actions {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 12px;
    margin-top: 26px;
  }
  .access-note {
    font-size: 13px;
    color: var(--muted);
    margin-top: 13px;
  }
  .memo-example {
    min-width: 0;
  }
  .memo-example .sheet {
    border-color: var(--ink);
    box-shadow: 0 16px 36px var(--shadow);
  }
  .sheet-bar {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 8px;
    border-bottom-color: var(--ink);
    padding-inline: 16px;
  }
  .example-name {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 8px;
    padding: 14px 24px;
    border-bottom: 3px double var(--ink);
    font: 12px/1.5 var(--font-mono);
  }
  .example-name span {
    color: var(--muted);
  }
  .memo-body {
    padding: 26px 24px 30px;
  }
  .memo-body h2 {
    font-size: 28px;
    line-height: 1.2;
    margin-bottom: 21px;
  }
  .memo-body p {
    font-size: 15px;
  }
  .memo-body p + p {
    margin-top: 13px;
  }
  figcaption {
    font-size: 12px;
    color: var(--muted);
    margin-top: 14px;
    max-width: 52ch;
  }
  .assistant-strip {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 12px 28px;
    border-block: 1px solid var(--hairline);
    padding-block: 22px;
    font-size: 13px;
    color: var(--muted);
  }
  .assistant-strip strong {
    color: var(--ink);
    font-weight: 500;
  }
  .section {
    padding-block: 80px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--hairline);
  }
  .section h2 {
    font-size: clamp(32px, 4vw, 48px);
    margin-block: 16px 24px;
  }
  .section h2 span {
    color: var(--muted);
  }
  .section-lead {
    max-width: 60ch;
    margin-bottom: 32px;
    font-size: 18px;
  }
  .use-cases,
  .controls {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 32px;
  }
  .use-case {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--hairline);
    padding: 32px;
    border-radius: 16px;
  }
  h3 {
    font-size: 26px;
    margin-bottom: 12px;
  }
  .use-case p,
  .controls p {
    color: var(--muted);
  }
  .use-case .sample-rule {
    margin-top: 24px;
    padding-top: 20px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--hairline);
    color: var(--ink);
    font-size: 15px;
  }
  .steps {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 32px;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 32px 0;
    list-style: none;
    counter-reset: step;
  }
  .steps li {
    counter-increment: step;
  }
  .steps li::before {
    content: "0" counter(step);
    font: 12px/1.5 var(--font-mono);
    color: var(--muted);
  }
  .steps h3 {
    margin-top: 16px;
  }
  .steps p {
    color: var(--muted);
  }
  code {
    font-size: 13px;
  }
  .reading-note {
    max-width: 75ch;
    margin-top: 32px;
    font-size: 13px;
    color: var(--muted);
  }
  .control-section {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 0.8fr 1fr;
    gap: 64px;
  }
  .controls {
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    gap: 32px;
  }
  .faq details {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--hairline);
    padding-block: 12px;
  }
  .faq summary {
    cursor: pointer;
    min-height: 44px;
    padding-block: 10px;
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .faq details p {
    max-width: 75ch;
    margin-block: 8px 12px;
    color: var(--muted);
  }
  .closing {
    text-align: center;
    padding-block: 80px;
  }
  .closing h2 {
    font-size: clamp(32px, 4vw, 48px);
    margin-block: 16px;
  }
  .closing p:not(.eyebrow) {
    color: var(--muted);
    margin-bottom: 24px;
  }
  @media (min-width: 861px) and (max-width: 1100px) {
    .hero {
      gap: 32px;
      padding-block: 56px;
    }
  }
  @media (max-width: 960px) {
    h1 {
      max-width: 660px;
    }
    .intro {
      max-width: 45ch;
    }
    .memo-example {
      max-width: 600px;
    }
    .control-section {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 16px;
    }
  }
  @media (max-width: 860px) {
    .hero {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 38px;
      padding-block: 48px;
    }
  }
  @media (max-width: 767px) {
    .section,
    .closing {
      padding-block: 48px;
    }
    .use-cases,
    .steps {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 24px;
    }
    .hero {
      padding-block: 38px 44px;
      gap: 34px;
    }
    .eyebrow {
      font-size: 11px;
    }
    .intro {
      font-size: 17px;
      margin-top: 20px;
    }
    .actions {
      gap: 10px;
      margin-top: 22px;
    }
    .actions .button {
      font-size: 14px;
      padding-inline: 18px;
    }
    .sheet-bar {
      font-size: 10px;
      padding-inline: 12px;
    }
    .example-name {
      padding-inline: 18px;
    }
    .memo-body {
      padding: 22px 18px 25px;
    }
    .memo-body h2 {
      font-size: 25px;
    }
    .memo-body p {
      font-size: 14px;
    }
    .section-lead {
      font-size: 16px;
    }
    .use-case {
      padding: 24px;
    }
  }
</style>
